# Where Questions and Answers Are Stored

**Question storage:**
```json
{
  "question": {
    "id": "q_12345",
    "content": "encrypted_content",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "options": [
      {"id": "a", "text": "encrypted"},
      {"id": "b", "text": "encrypted"}
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "hashed_reference",
    "points": 5,
    "authorId": "teacher_67890"
  }
}
```

**Answer storage:**
```json
{
  "answer": {
    "id": "a_98765",
    "questionId": "q_12345",
    "studentId": "student_11111",
    "examId": "exam_22222",
    "response": "b",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:30:00Z",
    "ipAddress": "192.168.1.100",
    "isValidated": true
  }
}
```

# What Is Sent to the Client During an Exam

When a student starts an exam, the client receives:

```json
{
  "examSession": {
    "examId": "exam_22222",
    "studentId": "student_11111",
    "startTime": "2026-10-08T10:00:00Z",
    "endTime": "2026-10-08T11:00:00Z",
    "questions": [
      {
        "id": "q_12345",
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "encryptedContent": "base64_encrypted",
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "encrypted": "base64_encrypted"},
          {"id": "b", "encrypted": "base64_encrypted"}
        ]
      }
    ],
    "settings": {
      "allowReview": false,
      "showResults": "after_exam"
    }
  }
}
```

**Security features:**
- Questions are encrypted
- Correct answers are never sent to client
- Time validation enforced server-side
